# The release tarball is built on Linux by the publish workflow, so the files it reads must be
# byte-stable across checkouts. Without this, a Windows checkout rewrites the workflow and the
# shell scripts to CRLF, and the blob that ships differs from the one that was rehearsed.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
